course: dictionary
lesson: 8307
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning the writer wants. Roadrunner is one of these words: it can mean a real bird, or the cartoon bird from the old films.
explain: Look for clue words. In «A real roadrunner can run at about 30 km per hour, but a real coyote can run about twice as fast», the word real tells you the writer means the actual bird, not the cartoon. Always ask: is this sentence about a real thing or a story?
explain: The capital letters are another clue. The Road Runner, with capitals, is the name of a cartoon character. Once you know which meaning is used, you can read the sentence with confidence.
fact: A roadrunner is a fast bird of the deserts of the south-western USA and Mexico.
fact: A real roadrunner would rather run than fly, and it can run at about 30 km per hour.
fact: The Road Runner is a cartoon bird who always escapes from a hungry coyote.
fact: Real roadrunners do not say «meep meep»; they make soft cooing sounds and loud rattles by clattering their beaks.
fact: A real coyote can run about twice as fast as a roadrunner, so sometimes a coyote does catch one.
exercise: «A real roadrunner can run at about 30 km per hour.» How fast can a real roadrunner run? | About 3 km per hour, like a slow walk | It cannot run at all | About 300 km per hour | *About 30 km per hour
exercise: Which word in «The real greater roadrunner is a desert bird» tells you the writer means the actual bird? | *real | desert | bird | greater
exercise: «The Road Runner is a cartoon bird who always escapes from a hungry coyote.» What does the word cartoon tell you? | The bird is a real bird from the desert | The bird lives in the sea | The bird is a coyote | *The bird is from a drawn story, not a real bird
test: «Real roadrunners do not say meep meep; they make soft cooing sounds.» What do real roadrunners make instead of meep meep? | Meep meep | Loud barks | *Soft cooing sounds | Long howls
test: Which animal can run about twice as fast as a real roadrunner? | A bush | A snake | *A coyote | A lizard
exam: Jayden says, «Roadrunners go meep meep.» What is the best reply? | Roadrunners are fish that swim in the sea | *Only the cartoon bird says meep meep; real roadrunners make cooing sounds | Real roadrunners say meep meep when they run | Roadrunners cannot make any sound at all
